\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Windsor P. Lyon</a> owned and operated a mercantile store with his brother Carlos Lyon on the corner of Main and Hotchkiss streets in <a href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Nauvoo</a>. (“The Latter Day Saints,” <span class=\"title\">Times and Seasons,</span> 15 June 1841, 2:454; “Second Arrival,” <span class=\"title\">Nauvoo Neighbor,</span> 2 Aug. 1843, [4]; “Guide to Health,” <span class=\"title\">Times and Seasons,</span> 15 Jan. 1842, 3:669; <a href=\"/paper-summary/ordinance-27-november-1841-a\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/ordinance-27-november-1841-a\" poptitle=\"Ordinance, 27 November 1841–A\">“An Ordinance Concerning Fire Arms and Parties Litigant,” 27 Nov. 1841</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/ordinance-5-march-1842-b\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/ordinance-5-march-1842-b\" poptitle=\"Ordinance, 5 March 1842–B\">“An Ordinance in Relation to the Registry of Deeds, and Other Instruments of Writing,” 5 Mar. 1842</a>, Nauvoo, IL, Records, CHL; see also <a href=\"/paper-summary/affidavit-from-carlos-lyon-20-june-1844\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/affidavit-from-carlos-lyon-20-june-1844\" poptitle=\"Affidavit from Carlos Lyon, 20 June 1844\">Carlos W. Lyon, Affidavit, Nauvoo, IL, 20 June 1844</a>, JS Office Papers, CHL.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"> <span class=\"title\">Times and Seasons.</span> Commerce/Nauvoo, IL. Nov. 1839–Feb. 1846.</p><p id=\"source-note2\"> <span class=\"title\">Nauvoo Neighbor.</span> Nauvoo, IL. 1843–1845. </p></div></div></div></aside></td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83635\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8767324257495268513\"><a href=\"#8767324257495268513\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans22\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschr